    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Use this plugin to automatically run the OPTIMIZE command on your WordPress database every day. There are no settings to configure. Simply activate the plugin and you&#8217;re set!</p>\n<p>This plugin hooks into the existing WordPress cron system.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the <code>optimize-database</code> folder to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; menu in WordPress</li>\n<li>Enjoy!</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"when%20does%20the%20cron%20run%3F\">\nWhen does the cron run?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>The cron is set to run every day at the time you activated the plugin.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.6</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Requires PHP 7.4.</li>\n<li>Tested up to WordPress 6.9.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.5</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested up to WordPress 6.9.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.4</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested up to WordPress 5.6.</li>\n<li>Implement namespace.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.3</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested up to WordPress 5.0.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.2</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested up to WordPress 4.4.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested up to WordPress 4.0.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial version.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Automatically optimize your database daily.",
